      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(whatsapp): add chunk-idle timeout to inbound media download",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where WhatsApp inbound media downloads that stall after Baileys returns a stream (headers/start ok, then no further chunks) would block `downloadInboundMedia` forever via `saveMediaStream`'s unbounded `for await`, so inbound dispatch never produces an agent reply for that message.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Wrap the Baileys AsyncIterable with a local per-chunk idle race (production default `30_000` ms), matching Telegram's download idle floor and the LINE channel pattern (open `#86873`, different owner).\n- On timeout, reject with `WhatsAppInboundMediaTimeoutError`, call `iterator.return()` so Node Readable streams are destroyed, and silence the losing `next()` to avoid `unhandledRejection`.\n- Tests may pass a short `chunkTimeoutMs`; production omits it and uses the 30s floor (proven with fake timers).\n- Does **not** change core `saveMediaStream` / `src/media/store.ts` (avoids competing with LINE `#86873`).\n- Timeout error class stays module-private (knip unused-export gate).\n\nNo new config/env surface.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** A stalled WhatsApp media body could hang inbound handling for that message indefinitely.\n\n**After:** Idle streams fail closed after 30s with a clear timeout error so the monitor loop can continue.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCompete: no open WhatsApp-same-site PR; LINE `#86873` is a sibling pattern on a different channel.\n\nHead: `420f7f358ca0eb4c3439b8fce6700e259102a92a`\n\n```text\n$ OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/whatsapp/src/inbound/media.node.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n[whatsapp media idle proof] timed_out=true elapsed_ms=51 chunkTimeoutMs=50 production_ms=30000\n[whatsapp media idle proof] production_default_ms=30000 timed_out=true\nTests  15 passed (15)\n```\n\nNegative control: never-yielding stream without idle wrap would hang `saveMediaStream`'s `for await`; with the 50ms test floor, timeout rejects in ~51ms and `iterator.return()` is called once. Production default path advances fake timers to 30s and rejects with `chunkTimeoutMs: 30000`.\n\nCI follow-up: fixed oxlint `no-promise-executor-return` / `use-unknown-in-catch-callback-variable`, and removed unused exported timeout symbols that failed `check-dependencies`.",
